        "message": "Here are three practical ways to set that boundary while living together: 1. **Use a consistent, low-energy response.** Give a short, closed answer every time it comes up—something like, \"Nothing new, and I prefer to keep that part of my life private.\" Keeping your tone flat and predictable makes the topic boring to pursue.\n2. **Pivot immediately to ordinary household topics.** Pair your boundary with a quick subject change: \"No updates there. By the way, do we need anything from the grocery store?\" This signals that the dating discussion is over without turning it into a confrontation.\n3. **Have an exit ready.** If they keep pressing, excuse yourself politely rather than explaining or defending your choice. Stepping into your room or running an errand creates physical space without needing an argument. You can try out whichever approach feels most natural to hold, or adapt the wording to how you normally talk to them.",
